// ALLOWED-DRIFT: legacy regex linter skipped the SELECT-list aggregate rule when the list contained a subquery (a heuristic to dodge a lazy `.*?\s+FROM\b` mis-capture). The CST walker flags the subquery AND recurses to flag the inner aggregate; both are independently correct (parser stricter).

